WHY THIS LICENCE. It matches the licence of the model output the work is
built on (Cerpa et al. 2022, doi:10.5281/zenodo.6817177, CC BY 4.0), so
the whole chain from model output to published figure carries the same
attribution requirement.

NOTE ON SOFTWARE. Creative Commons does not recommend CC licences for
source code, because they address neither patent rights nor the
source/object distinction that software licences handle. The choice here
is deliberate: this repository is a post-processing analysis published
alongside a paper, not a software product, and consistency with the data
licence was preferred. If you wish to reuse the code in a context where a
conventional software licence matters, contact the author.

THE BUNDLED MODEL OUTPUT IN data/ IS NOT COVERED BY THIS NOTICE. It is
redistributed from Cerpa et al. (2022) under their own CC BY 4.0 licence;
see data/ATTRIBUTION.md. Cite them, not this repository, for the data.
